The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (mi != NULL) {
    _ncesmp = mi->n_elts;
    _icetsm = mi->elt_id;
}
_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays(f->id, &_itpsmp, &_smcelp);
```
Reason:
The absence of braces around the conditional block means that only the first line (`_ncesmp = mi->n_elts;`) is executed if `mi` is not NULL. This can lead to `_icetsm` being uninitialized when `_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays` is called, potentially causing a crash due to accessing a NULL pointer.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
_volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays(f->id, &_itpsmp, &_smcelp);
if (_ncesmp > 0)
    _volume_mass_injection_get_field_arrays(CS_F_(p)->id, NULL, &_gamma);
```
Reason:
The patch ensures that the function calls are properly executed based on the state of `_ncesmp`. By removing the braces and ensuring that the function calls are executed only when the conditions are met, it prevents the access of uninitialized pointers, thus avoiding the crash.

